{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zo3zjlk2wpqtgygezrmcjwfnmf2zkpu5veaphdkqc32e4onoknfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is correct — no divergence from the C found.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — `nm -D --defined-only` sets are *identical* (`printLine`, `bad`, `good`, `driver`); 0 missing. No untranslated C module: `c_src` is one 68-line TU, fully translated. `nm -D -u` shows only libc/libunwind imports. The two `static` C helpers correctly stay out of the dynamic symbol table.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all 24 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass (24 tests, seeded PRNG).\n- [x] **Binary stdout** — vacuous: `CMakeLists.txt` has no `add_executable`, Cargo has no `[[bin]]`. Replaced with the stronger per-call fd-1 capture.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all 15 `ERRORS.md` rows pass (12 tests; row 10 documented as untestable UB, not checked off).\n- [x] **All feature combos** — Cargo declares no `[features]`; `{default, --no-default-features}` × `{debug, release}` all green (39/39 each).\n\n## Two real issues I found and fixed in the test infrastructure\n\n1. **False-pass risk (important):** `cargo test` does *not* build the `cdylib` artifact. My first harness searched profile dirs permissively, so the debug run silently loaded the **release** `.so` and reported a pass for a profile never exercised. Fixed: the harness now derives the `.so` strictly from the test binary's own `target/<profile>/`, hard-fails if absent, and `phase_d_audit_loaded_libraries` asserts the loaded path matches `cfg!(debug_assertions)`. `scripts/all_features.sh` now runs `cargo build` per profile/combo first.\n2. **Unverified claim in the source comments.** `lib.rs` asserted `helperBad` returns NULL \"verified at -O0 and -O2\". At `-O1`+ GCC inlines `helperBad`, so no such symbol exists to inspect — the claim wasn't checkable as written. I verified it behaviorally instead (`scripts/opt_levels.sh`): the C's `bad()` emits **nothing** at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os` and the reference cmake build, matching Rust in both profiles.\n\n## Coverage worth noting\n\nThe C's `printf(\"%s\\n\", line)` is rewritten by GCC to `puts` — and rustc independently emits the same `puts` call, so buffering mode and bytes match, not just content. Tests specifically pin the behaviors a careless translation would break: invalid UTF-8 and high/negative `char` bytes pass through verbatim (a `str`-based translation would panic), payloads containing `%n`/`%s` are never interpreted as format strings, interior NULs truncate, and `driver` treats *every* non-zero `int` — including `i32::MIN` and out-of-range \"enum\" values like `255` — as true, with only exact `0` selecting `bad()`. Row 13 also calls `driver` through a 64-bit-arg signature to confirm only `%edi` is read.\n\nThe one place the C is UB (CWE-562, returning a dangling stack pointer) is reproduced rather than \"fixed\": `bad()` prints nothing in both, and tests assert `\"helperBad string\"` never reaches stdout.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified; the only file changed under `translation/` was `Cargo.toml` (adding the `libloading` dev-dependency). `libloading` came from the local cargo cache via `--offline`, since crates.io is blocked by the sandbox proxy."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":850,"cache_read_input_tokens":88204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":850,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c286b925-262c-452e-8956-c5f3ac18d64c","uuid":"e498d6e4-f6d2-48bf-b38e-591d57b3fca3","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:42:35.842Z"}
